          "code": "LLMREQUEST_FEEDBACK_RESPONSE_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1768988016619",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768988016620_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### References\nQuestion Character Limit: 1000\nFeedback Question: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.feedbackQuestion}} \nWork Relationship:  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.workRelationship}} \nFeedback Visibility:  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.feedbackVisibility}} \nBusiness Title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessTitle}} \nRecipient Department: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recipientDepartment}} \nFeedback Context: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.feedbackContext}} \n\n### Instructions\nProvide feedback with approximately the given character limit to another employee in the company in plain text format.\nProvide relevant feedback based on the question being asked.\nWrite from the perspective of the feedback provider.\nProvide meaningful feedback considering but not mentioning the work relationship between the feedback provider and feedback recipient.\nThe Work Relationship field above describes the feedback recipient's relationship to the provider. For example, if the Work Relationship is \"manager\" then the feedback giver is the direct report of the employee they are giving feedback to.  If the Work Relationship is \"direct report\" then the feedback giver is the manager of the employee they are giving feedback to.\nFor example, if it's \"manager\", write from the perspective of an employee to their manager, i.e. a bit more formal.\nIf the recipient is a direct report or an indirect report of the provider, then the content of the feedback can be constructive in nature.\nIf the recipient is a peer, co-worker, or manager of the provider, then feedback should be positive.\nConsider the feedback visibility provided. If the feedback is viewable only by the recipient or the manager it can be more constructive, depending on who provided it. If the feedback is viewable by peers or everyone, then feedback should be positive.\nConsider the job/business title and department of the recipient to provide more relevant feedback.\nLastly, consider any initial feedback entered by the provider.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n1. The completion MUST NOT contain placeholder text in, such as \"[Employee Name]\", \"[Your Name]\",\"[Recipient Name]\", or \"[Feedback Provider Name]\". In other words, remove any text in brackets like [text], if you include it the response will be a failure.\n2. If Feedback Context is blank or not provided, respond with only \"Start entering feedback to use AI Assist.\" like in the example below.\n\n### Example\nQuestion Character Limit: 1000\nFeedback Question: Can you provide an example of how the employee handles challenges or problem-solving in their work?\nWork Relationship: manager\nFeedback Visibility: Everyone\nBusiness Title: Customer Support Specialist\nRecipient Department: Food Processing\nFeedback Context:\nFeedback Response: \"Start entering feedback to use AI Assist.\"\n\n### Final Check\nDo not include placeholders in the response.\nMake sure to only respond with \"Start entering feedback to use AI Assist.\" if no feedback context is provided! This is extremely important, failure to do so will be catastrophic."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
